# This repository publishes the system, the evidence and the verifier. It does
# not publish the manuscript-facing analysis pipeline: the scripts that recompute
# the paper's numbers from the journals, the generated tables and figures they
# write, the bibliography they check, the test suite, the JSON schemas and the
# longer-form notes are all held back here deliberately and are ignored below
# rather than merely absent, so that a stray `git add .` cannot reintroduce them.
#
# The consequence is worth stating plainly rather than discovering later: what
# remains is reproducible in the sense that the journals under artifacts/ are the
# recorded evidence and every run in them can be verified from a clean checkout,
# but the published tree cannot by itself re-derive a table in the paper. The
# README says the same thing where a reader will meet it.

# Held back from the published artifact. On disk, out of the index.
docs/
figures/
schemas/
scripts/
tables/
tests/
refs.bib
SECURITY.md
THIRD_PARTY.md
CITATION.cff
CONTRIBUTING.md
environment-tested.txt

# Credentials. Never commit these. The .example files are the templates a user
# fills in locally, so they are negated back in after the wildcard above them,
# and the negation must stay a "!" rather than becoming a comment.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
deploy/azure/deploy.env
!deploy/azure/deploy.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Output written by a fresh reproduction run. The committed journals under
# artifacts/ are the paper's evidence; a local re-run writes here instead of
# overwriting them, and must not be committed on top of them.
artifacts/local/
artifacts/runtime/
artifacts/preview*
artifacts/run-*/
*.pcap

# Editor and OS noise
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
